specs/map-landscape-quality/exploration.md:40:- The shared water helper returned linear albedo, but the terrain material converted the blended water a second time. The material now converts dry terrain first and blends water in linear space. A matched consumer fixture exposes the previous mismatch.
specs/map-landscape-quality/slices/15-acceptance.md:17:Production campaign and battle, final screenshot/crop set, water motion GIF, and archived full-game hardware report.
specs/map-landscape-quality/README.md:25:- [ ] [09 — Shared water depth, surf and motion](slices/09-water-response.md)
specs/map-landscape-quality/slices/09-water-response.md:1:# 09 — Shared water depth, surf and motion
specs/map-landscape-quality/slices/09-water-response.md:13:Feed independent coverage, signed shore distance and depth/proxy inputs into the shared response. Give campaign sea visible turquoise shallows and deeper offshore color rather than reusing the bounded battle field-water ramp. Add broken shore surf and restrained normal/motion detail tied to the canonical water domain; rivers and lakes use appropriate profiles of the same response. Preserve exactly one linear conversion and one light/environment source. Mask every effect so it cannot sparkle on land. All animation uses the owned injectable clock.
specs/map-landscape-quality/slices/09-water-response.md:17:Planned landscape-water scene, retaining terrain-water; fixed near/deep/shore crops plus a short frozen-time sequence and looping GIF. Include a battle field-water/ocean boundary.
specs/map-landscape-quality/slices/09-water-response.md:31:Depth ramps, wave/foam amplitudes, wavelengths and normal detail falloff are delegated within the water and performance contracts. No second sea shader or unowned time source.
specs/map-landscape-quality/architecture.md:50:Convert display-authored dry albedo exactly once; common water response is already linear. Share roughness/normal/light response while exposing scale-specific depth and detail inputs. Waves use the owned frame time and remain inside their water body.
specs/map-landscape-quality/slices/05-terrain-material.md:23:Crop/mask: Lit/shaded rock face, grass shelf and scree-foot crops. Geometry, tree model/placement, lighting, water shape and wave motion are frozen.
